2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:09,280
Daniel has also found a talk about why wild animals are in danger.

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:13,950
Listen with him and complete the notes below.

4
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:18,560
Wild animals are in danger for many reasons.

5
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,780
One reason is natural.

6
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:30,900
For example, it is difficult for some special kinds of wild animals to have babies and they may get sick easily and die.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:36,830
Natural disasters like floods can also be a problem for wild animals.

8
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:41,150
However, human activities are the biggest reason.

9
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:48,610
People take lots of land for their own use so many animals lose their living spaces.

10
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:56,210
Air pollution and water pollution also make it difficult for animals to live healthy lives.

11
00:00:56,210 --> 00:01:04,300
Moreover, human activities are warming the earth and serious weather events happen more often.

12
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:11,990
As a result, certain wild animals may not have a place to live or enough food to eat.

13
00:01:11,990 --> 00:01:16,520
Hunting is another big problem for wild animals.

14
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:22,510
People hunt them for food and their fur, bones or other parts of the body.

15
00:01:22,510 --> 00:01:27,180
All of these make it hard for animals to survive in the wild.
